extend type Query {
  """
  Configured producers and consumers of one item or fluid for a force on a surface, from a single-tick snapshot of
  assembling machines, furnaces, rocket silos and mining drills plus every burner entity, optionally bounded by area and
  sorted by name, position and unit number. Producers are machines whose current, or for furnaces previous, recipe or
  mining target yields the item; consumers are machines whose recipe or mining target consumes it, plus burner entities
  that use the item as fuel. Limit (1..10000) and zero-based offset slice each list independently but with the same
  window, and producerPageInfo/consumerPageInfo each count their full pre-pagination match set. Rates are theoretical
  expected base yields at current machine speed — crafting_speed/recipe energy times the expected product amount, or
  mining_speed times (1+speed_bonus)/mining_time — excluding productivity, quality upgrades, downtime, power or fuel
  shortages, blocked output and depletion, so they are not observed throughput; infinite resources and uncomputable
  cases return null theoreticalRatePerSecond with rateUnavailableReason. role marks RECIPE endpoints (recipe or mining
  target based) and FUEL endpoints (burner fuel consumption); FUEL rows use
  max_energy_usage*60*(1+consumption_bonus)/(fuel_value*effectivity) at full duty, an upper bound, and set rateBasis
  FUEL_UPPER_BOUND. Furnaces whose current recipe is unset fall back to previous_recipe, reported with recipeSource
  PREVIOUS and rateBasis IDLE_PREVIOUS_RECIPE_POTENTIAL because the reported rate is the idle furnace's potential, not
  observed output; furnaces with neither recipe cannot be matched to an item and are absent. bufferedItems counts only
  the matching item in that role's inventory (crafter input for recipe consumers, fuel inventory for FUEL consumers,
  output inventory for producers), never whole-machine or factory stock; bufferedFluidAmount sums only role-compatible
  fluidbox contents and is null for items. status is the engine entity status name; empty or unknown force/surface
  names, an item name that is neither an item nor fluid prototype, or out-of-range limit/offset produce a GraphQL error,
  and empty lists mean no machine matched in the area.
  """
  itemFlow(input: ItemFlowInput!): ItemFlow!
  """
  Deterministic recursive material plan for one item, quality and amount, computed in Go from a single snapshot of the
  force's recipe catalogue and an explicit stock source. FACTORY stock sums inventories of containers, crafting machines
  (input, output, modules, trash and dump), furnaces, silos, labs, cargo wagons, car and spider trunks, inserter hands,
  belt and loader lines and all fluidboxes inside the optional area, capped at 50000 entities and 20000 recipes; PLAYER
  stock is the named player's main inventory only, must exist on the requested force and surface, and forbids area.
  Truncated stock, a truncated recipe catalogue or an unresolved recipe cycle makes complete false, belt-line
  deduplication stops after 20 million comparisons with stockTruncated set, and mined, gathered or fluid raw materials
  are not consumed by the plan. The catalogue keeps enabled, non-hidden recipes only: recycling and parameter recipes are
  excluded so a plan never satisfies demand with an item's own recycling recipe, and recipes that exist but are not
  researched are reported as RECIPE_NOT_RESEARCHED instead of being planned. Recipes are matched by output item with
  exact-name recipes preferred over lexicographic order, may be overridden per item (at most 20000, duplicates rejected),
  and are expanded depth-first with maxDepth 1..512 and maxExpansions 1..100000; an exhausted expansion budget is
  reported as explicit unresolved demand. availableStock/allocatedStock are one shared pool, so materials, steps,
  rawRequirements, seedRequirements (catalysts needing initial stock) and unresolved together are an expected-value
  plan, not a globally optimal schedule or a craftability, machine, energy or transport claim; probabilistic yields
  become expected values flagged by probabilistic. Invalid amount (non-finite, non-positive or above 1e12), missing or
  inconsistent stock source, unknown quality, unknown or ambiguous item/fluid prototype, or invalid override produce a
  GraphQL error.
  """
  billOfMaterials(input: BillOfMaterialsInput!): BillOfMaterials!
  """
  One-call answer to "is this item short, and who starves", composing three reads: itemFlow for configured producers and
  consumers of the item, the item and fluid flow statistics for the requested window, and the same item-filtered stock
  scan as stock. producedPerMinute/consumedPerMinute are observed force flow statistics for the whole surface over the
  window, not this factory block; theoreticalSupply/theoreticalDemand sum the itemFlow theoretical rates of every
  producer and consumer and are potentials, not measurements; net is observed production minus observed consumption and
  can differ in sign and magnitude from theoretical demand minus supply. stock totals every counted factory, ground,
  belt and player inventory row for the item, grouped by stock category, and ignores fuel, modules and equipment exactly
  like stock. producers and consumers come from the itemFlow scan without its pagination arguments: they are capped at
  1000 rows each and truncated is true when either list was cut, so partial lists never look complete.
  starvedConsumers holds only consumers that are short of this item: FUEL consumers whose fuel inventory holds none of
  it, even if they are still burning stored fuel, or that report no_fuel, and RECIPE consumers reporting missing
  ingredients or fuel. A consumer blocked on an unrelated condition (depleted resources, no power, full output,
  disabled) is never listed just for that status, so a drill with coal in its fuel inventory cannot appear as starved. Burner FUEL rates are upper bounds
  and idle furnaces contribute their previous-recipe potential, so theoretical demand can exceed observed consumption.
  Empty, unknown or ambiguous force/surface/item names, an invalid window, or invalid area bounds produce a GraphQL
  error; the query reads only engine state and emits no notification.
  """
  itemBalance(input: ItemBalanceInput!): ItemBalance!
}

input ItemFlowInput {
  force: String! = "player"
  surface: String! = "nauvis"
  item: String!
  area: FactoryAreaInput
  limit: Int! = 100
  offset: Int! = 0
}

type ItemFlow {
  tick: Float!
  force: String!
  surface: String!
  item: String!
  producerPageInfo: PageInfo!
  consumerPageInfo: PageInfo!
  producers: [ItemFlowEndpoint!]!
  consumers: [ItemFlowEndpoint!]!
  rateAssumptions: String!
}

"""RECIPE covers recipe- and mining-target-based endpoints; FUEL marks a burner that consumes the item as fuel."""
enum ItemFlowRole { RECIPE FUEL }
"""CURRENT is the recipe the machine holds now; PREVIOUS is an idle furnace's remembered recipe."""
enum RecipeSource { CURRENT PREVIOUS }

type ItemFlowEndpoint {
  unitNumber: UnitNumber
  name: String!
  type: String!
  surface: String!
  force: String!
  position: Position!
  status: String!
  """RECIPE for recipe or mining-target matches, FUEL for burner fuel consumption."""
  role: ItemFlowRole!
  recipe: String
  recipeQuality: String
  """CURRENT when the machine holds this recipe now, PREVIOUS when an idle furnace only remembers it, null for mining or fuel endpoints."""
  recipeSource: RecipeSource
  miningTarget: String
  materialType: String!
  """Matching item stacks in only this role's input/output/fuel inventory; never whole-factory stock."""
  bufferedItems: [InventoryStack!]!
  """Matching fluid in role-compatible fluidboxes; null for items."""
  bufferedFluidAmount: Float
  """Expected units/second at current speed, excluding productivity and quality upgrades. Null when uncomputable, including infinite mining resources."""
  theoreticalRatePerSecond: Float
  """Why the rate is an approximation rather than an instantaneous expectation: FUEL_UPPER_BOUND for burner fuel at full duty, IDLE_PREVIOUS_RECIPE_POTENTIAL for an idle furnace's remembered recipe. Null when the rate is the plain theoretical expectation."""
  rateBasis: String
  rateUnavailableReason: String
}

"""Surface and force must be non-empty names of existing objects; item must be exactly one item or fluid prototype."""
input ItemBalanceInput {
  force: String! = "player"
  surface: String! = "nauvis"
  item: String!
  """Flow-statistics window; ONE_MINUTE, TEN_MINUTES or ONE_HOUR."""
  window: ProductionWindow! = ONE_MINUTE
  """Optional finite bounds; left/top must not exceed right/bottom. Omit to scan the surface."""
  area: FactoryAreaInput
}

type ItemBalance {
  tick: Float!
  force: String!
  surface: String!
  item: String!
  window: ProductionWindow!
  """Observed production for the whole surface and force over the window, from flow statistics."""
  producedPerMinute: Float!
  """Observed consumption for the whole surface and force over the window, from flow statistics."""
  consumedPerMinute: Float!
  """Sum of itemFlow producer rates times 60: a potential, not measured supply."""
  theoreticalSupply: Float!
  """Sum of itemFlow consumer rates times 60: a potential upper bound, not measured demand."""
  theoreticalDemand: Float!
  """producedPerMinute minus consumedPerMinute, from observed statistics only."""
  net: Float!
  stock: ItemBalanceStock!
  producers: [ItemFlowEndpoint!]!
  consumers: [ItemFlowEndpoint!]!
  """Consumers that are short of this item specifically: FUEL consumers whose fuel inventory holds none of it or that report no_fuel, and RECIPE consumers reporting missing ingredients or fuel. Consumers blocked on an unrelated condition such as no_minable_resources, no_power or full_output are excluded unless their own inventory for this item is empty."""
  starvedConsumers: [ItemFlowEndpoint!]!
  """True when producers or consumers were cut at the 1000-row scan limit, so the lists are partial."""
  truncated: Boolean!
  assumptions: String!
}

type ItemBalanceStock {
  """Sum of every counted stock row for the item, independent of pagination."""
  total: Float!
  byCategory: [ItemBalanceCategory!]!
}

type ItemBalanceCategory {
  """Stock category name: stored, in-transit, ground, player or worker."""
  category: String!
  count: Float!
}

enum BOMStockSource { FACTORY PLAYER }
input BOMStockInput {
  source: BOMStockSource!
  """Required only for PLAYER. Main inventory only, same force and surface required."""
  player: String
  """Optional FACTORY scan bounds, at most 1024 tiles per side."""
  area: FactoryAreaInput
}
input BOMRecipeOverrideInput { item: String! recipe: String! }
input BillOfMaterialsInput {
  force: String! = "player"
  surface: String! = "nauvis"
  item: String!
  """Finite positive target quantity, at most 1e12."""
  amount: Float!
  quality: String! = "normal"
  stock: BOMStockInput!
  recipeOverrides: [BOMRecipeOverrideInput!]
  """1..512 dependency levels."""
  maxDepth: Int! = 64
  """1..100000 recursive allocations. Exhaustion is explicit unresolved demand."""
  maxExpansions: Int! = 2000
}

type BillOfMaterials {
  tick: Float!
  force: String!
  surface: String!
  item: String!
  amount: Float!
  quality: String!
  stockSource: BOMStockSource!
  """False when snapshot/expansion bounds or unresolved recipe cycles prevent full expansion. Missing mined/raw ingredients alone do not make expansion incomplete."""
  complete: Boolean!
  stockTruncated: Boolean!
  recipeCatalogueTruncated: Boolean!
  """Expected-value plan, not guaranteed outputs, when any selected recipe has probabilistic yields."""
  probabilistic: Boolean!
  expansions: Int!
  materials: [BOMMaterial!]!
  steps: [BOMStep!]!
  rawRequirements: [BOMRequirement!]!
  """Reused input/output catalysts need initial seed stock. Seeds are not consumed again or multiplied by craft count."""
  seedRequirements: [BOMRequirement!]!
  unresolved: [BOMRequirement!]!
  warnings: [String!]!
  assumptions: String!
}

type BOMMaterial {
  item: String!
  materialType: String!
  quality: String!
  required: Float!
  availableStock: Float!
  allocatedStock: Float!
  """Demand not covered by original stock, before recipes/coproducts; not a craftability claim."""
  missingStock: Float!
  expectedYield: Float!
  surplus: Float!
}

type BOMStep {
  recipe: String!
  item: String!
  materialType: String!
  quality: String!
  crafts: Float!
  """Net expected target output after cancelling this recipe's returned inputs."""
  expectedOutput: Float!
  alternatives: [String!]!
  overridden: Boolean!
}

type BOMRequirement {
  item: String!
  materialType: String!
  quality: String!
  amount: Float!
  """MINED_RAW (resource entity), GATHERED_RAW (tree, plant, simple-entity, fish or asteroid-chunk), RAW_FLUID (fluid with no recipe), RECIPE_NOT_RESEARCHED (a non-hidden recipe exists but is disabled), NO_ENABLED_RECIPE (nothing enabled produces it), or an explicit plan bound such as RECIPE_CYCLE, EXPANSION_LIMIT, CATALYST_SEED_MISSING, FLUID_TEMPERATURE_NOT_PLANNED, INVALID_RECIPE_YIELD or NUMERIC_BOUND_EXCEEDED."""
  reason: String!
}
